# FreedomOffice License Information

FreedomOffice is a fork of LibreOffice and is made available under the same
licensing terms as LibreOffice. Specifically, FreedomOffice is licensed under
a combination of the following licenses:

## Primary Licenses

### Mozilla Public License Version 2.0 (MPL-2.0)

Most source files in FreedomOffice are licensed under the Mozilla Public
License v2.0. A copy of the MPL-2.0 can be found in:

    freedomoffice-core/COPYING.MPL

The MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft license that allows the covered code to
be used in proprietary projects as long as the MPL-covered files remain under
the MPL. For full terms, see:

    https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/

### GNU Lesser General Public License Version 3.0 (LGPL-3.0)

Some libraries and components of FreedomOffice are licensed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License v3.0. A copy of the LGPL-3.0 can be found in:

    freedomoffice-core/COPYING.LGPL

The LGPL-3.0 allows the covered library to be linked into proprietary
applications. For full terms, see:

    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html

### GNU General Public License Version 3.0 (GPL-3.0)

Some components of FreedomOffice are licensed under the GNU General Public
License v3.0. A copy of the GPL-3.0 can be found in:

    freedomoffice-core/COPYING

For full terms, see:

    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

## Icon Theme License

The FreedomOffice Fluent Icon Theme (located in `freedomoffice-core/icon-themes/freedomoffice/`)
is based on the Colibre Icon Theme and is licensed under Creative Commons
CC0 1.0 Universal. See `freedomoffice-core/icon-themes/freedomoffice/COPYING-ICONS`
for details.

## Dual Licensing

As with LibreOffice, FreedomOffice components are generally available to you
under the MPL-2.0, with the option to distribute under the LGPL-3.0 or GPL-3.0
where applicable. Individual source files should contain license headers
indicating which license applies.

## How to Apply These Licenses

When creating new files for FreedomOffice, please add the appropriate MPL-2.0
license header to the top of each file. The standard header for new files is:

```
This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
```

